**Because the Voidwalker is a tank pet.**

Its Torment and Suffering abilities generate threat, keeping enemies focused on the pet instead of the squishy warlock. Combined with Sacrifice for a shield and Consume Shadows for healing, it lets warlocks pull multiple mobs and survive mistakes — making it far more forgiving for solo leveling.

The Succubus deals more damage but has *Soothing Kiss*, which **reduces** her threat — the opposite of what you want. She's fragile, and if mobs turn on the warlock (who wears cloth and has no defenses), death comes quickly. Using her effectively requires managing Seduction and careful pet control.

So while the Succubus is technically faster for skilled players, the Voidwalker's "set it and forget it" tanking makes it the default choice for most warlocks. [end of text]


